.TH NASD 8 "2026-05-13" "0.45.0" "KilasOS Administration Manual"
.SH NAME
nasd \- KilasOS NAS administration daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nasd
[\fB\-\-addr\fR \fIhost:port\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nasd
is the HTTP API and web UI daemon for KilasOS, a NAS operating system
built on Debian with ZFS.  It manages ZFS pools and datasets, Samba and
NFS shares, backup jobs (borg, restic, rclone), Docker containers and
compose stacks, system monitoring, and security auditing through a
single HTTPS interface.
.PP
The daemon requires root-equivalent privileges for ZFS and systemd
operations; these are delegated via a
.BR sudoers (5)
allowlist that restricts the
.B kilasos
service account to a fixed set of binaries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-addr\fR \fIhost:port\fR
Listen address.  Default:
.BR 0.0.0.0:8443 .
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and build information, then exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/kilasos/env
Environment file sourced by systemd before starting the daemon.
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/kilasos
NOPASSWD allowlist for the
.B kilasos
service account.
.TP
.I /var/lib/kilasos/
Persistent state directory (ZFS properties cache, backup job
definitions, alert rules, etc.).
.TP
.I /var/log/kilasos/
Audit and operational logs.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown: stops the HTTP listener, waits for in-flight
requests to complete, then exits.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR sudoers (5),
.BR zfs (8),
.BR zpool (8),
.BR smbd (8),
.BR borg (1),
.BR restic (1)
